// C round-trip for `chr` (DEC-020): astra_builtin_chr must build the 1-byte
// string and word the range guard exactly like the seed VM, so the compiled
// program's output and its bounds error are byte-identical to the VM route.
// The positive output is pinned by conformance/expressions/chr_basic.astra,
// which sweep_emit_c.sh runs through both backends; this twin pins the C
// runtime's bounds message with the `file:line:` prefix the harness requires.
// EXPECT-RUNTIME-ERROR: chr value 256 out of bounds (0..255)
fn main() {
    print(chr(256))
}
